nodecode-found is a rewrite of Utkarshkapil's Utkarshkapil/found-hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/Utkarshkapil/found-hermes-plugin
  commit 525b2bbfd02f5703253b260d2e1ac3af9c370e00
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Utkarsh Kapil (FOUND) (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the Agent Plugins package at that commit: plugin.json,
mcp.json and skills/found-outreach/SKILL.md. It declares no code, so what was
rewritten is its configuration and its skill. mcp.json names FOUND's hosted
server (https://app.foundtofind.com/mcp) and runs mcp-remote@0.1.49 through
npx to keep a browser-signed-in session; this cell speaks the same MCP
streamable-HTTP wire in Lisp (initialize, notifications/initialized,
tools/call, a session kept by Mcp-Session-Id, a JSON or event-stream answer
read either way) and needs no Node. The remote tool names are kept
(connect_status, find_leads, pipeline_stats, pipeline_breakdown,
campaign_report, compare_campaigns, prioritise_accounts, research_account,
draft_message, find_new_leads, find_contact_at_company, get_new_leads,
enrich_lead), gathered into six tools a model can pick between. The skill's
guidance is kept whole as (help :found): which tool answers which question,
found_status once near the start, the ids it answers, the signal behind each
lead, campaigns that start paused, the quote-then-confirm spend, and every
third_party and their_words field being someone else's words.

What was left out, and why: the browser sign-in, because mcp-remote is the
Node program this cell exists to replace -- the section carries the API key
the original README documents for servers and headless machines instead; the
npx launch and its token store under ~/.mcp-auth, which belong to that
program; and the five remote tools that write to the account (get_campaign,
create_campaign, update_sequence, add_to_list, add_to_campaign), which the
help topic names so the model points the user at FOUND's own app, but which
this cell does not wrap. The tool
set is served by FOUND at run time and is not covered by the pinned commit,
so a tool FOUND renames is reached here by the name it had at that commit.
LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
